# AWS Components

VPC

CIDR: 10.0.0.0/16

Provides network isolation for MediVault infrastructure.

Production Subnet

CIDR: 10.0.1.0/24

Hosts the MediVault EC2 application server.

Management Subnet

CIDR: 10.0.2.0/24

Reserved for infrastructure management and administrative access.

EC2

Hosts the MediVault application.

The EC2 instance will use EBS as its root storage.

S3

Stores medical scan images as objects.

S3 is an AWS managed object-storage service and does not receive a customer-assigned private IP address like an EC2 instance.

S3 Gateway VPC Endpoint

Provides private connectivity from the VPC to S3 without requiring a NAT Gateway.

IAM

Controls administrative and application access to AWS resources.

CloudWatch

Provides monitoring and metrics for the infrastructure.

