# Storage Design

The initial architecture uses two primary storage services:

EBS

Used by EC2 for:
Operating system
Application installation
Local application data where required

S3

Used for:
Medical scan images
Object-based application data

This separates compute/application storage from large-scale object storage.

# Security Principles

The architecture will follow:

Least-privilege IAM
Private S3 bucket
S3 Block Public Access
Encryption at rest
Encryption in transit
IAM Role for EC2-to-S3 access
Restricted administrative access